        <mxCell id="19" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#999999;spacing=8;" value="Link to the SSD and post-conditions: submitVoucher, submitVoucherUpdate and confirmArchive are the SSD messages that trigger the transitions.&#xa;Create: post-condition = a voucher exists with status Active and an audit record is written. Update: voucher details are changed and an audit record is written. Archive: status = Archived and the voucher cannot be applied to new orders.&#xa;If validation or saving fails, the state does not change and no voucher data is stored or changed.&#xa;Assumptions: Expired is derived from validUntil. An Expired voucher can be edited and becomes Active again when validUntil is moved to a date that is not in the past. Archived is final and read-only (UC3 activity diagram, Parts D and E)." vertex="1">
